    "delivery/delivery-1.json": "{\n  \"@context\": [\n    \"https://www.w3.org/ns/credentials/v2\",\n    \"https://rightsroot.org/spec/prm/ns/v1\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": [\n    \"VerifiableCredential\",\n    \"PRMDeliveryRecord\"\n  ],\n  \"noticeDigest\": \"uEiC5IVcL4rLIEItGi5JPCBeTyfp__1e7h9yL3Z_vJO3tRg\",\n  \"policyDigest\": \"uEiCCVYqo5goptwm4lS1RN_8WgOwJ5A8un4JTasreIyS9JA\",\n  \"recipient\": {\n    \"name\": \"City of Whittier Police Department\",\n    \"domain\": \"whittierpd.org\",\n    \"contact\": \"13200 Penn St\\nWhittier, CA 90602\"\n  },\n  \"method\": \"certified-mail\",\n  \"deliveredAt\": \"2026-09-17T16:00:00Z\",\n  \"recorded\": \"2026-09-17T17:00:00Z\",\n  \"reference\": \"PLACEHOLDER-TRACKING-0000\",\n  \"notes\": \"Certified mail, return receipt requested. Receipt retained privately.\",\n  \"proof\": {\n    \"type\": \"DataIntegrityProof\",\n    \"cryptosuite\": \"eddsa-jcs-2022\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-17T17:00:00Z\",\n    \"verificationMethod\": \"did:key:z6MkfCwPTWq3SKbw4AVj7j8t8oFBiFp6CvZiTnXAw24nVkLH#z6MkfCwPTWq3SKbw4AVj7j8t8oFBiFp6CvZiTnXAw24nVkLH\",\n    \"proofPurpose\": \"assertionMethod\",\n    \"proofValue\": \"zcuQqAy8z8zE8yHth23vwiJPbUUQRGZVaTqpsSZYp6fwfcnVdfRif75NdetQUSDcXnWgDaz5yNgtEtdAoGx1UoYr\"\n  },\n  \"id\": \"urn:prm:delivery:uEiDlNIKixXUb-zlvksppHXRGyPnP47Itkcrq_kyIoxK7Yw\"\n}",
    "response/response-1.json": "{\n  \"@context\": [\n    \"https://www.w3.org/ns/credentials/v2\",\n    \"https://rightsroot.org/spec/prm/ns/v1\"\n  ],\n  \"type\": [\n    \"VerifiableCredential\",\n    \"PRMResponseRecord\"\n  ],\n  \"noticeDigest\": \"uEiC5IVcL4rLIEItGi5JPCBeTyfp__1e7h9yL3Z_vJO3tRg\",\n  \"deliveryDigest\": \"uEiDlNIKixXUb-zlvksppHXRGyPnP47Itkcrq_kyIoxK7Yw\",\n  \"recipient\": {\n    \"name\": \"City of Whittier Police Department\"\n  },\n  \"status\": \"acknowledged\",\n  \"receivedAt\": \"2026-09-24T15:00:00Z\",\n  \"recorded\": \"2026-09-24T16:00:00Z\",\n  \"notes\": \"Placeholder: receipt acknowledged, no position stated on the individual objections.\",\n  \"proof\": {\n    \"type\": \"DataIntegrityProof\",\n    \"cryptosuite\": \"eddsa-jcs-2022\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-24T16:00:00Z\",\n    \"verificationMethod\": \"did:key:z6MkfCwPTWq3SKbw4AVj7j8t8oFBiFp6CvZiTnXAw24nVkLH#z6MkfCwPTWq3SKbw4AVj7j8t8oFBiFp6CvZiTnXAw24nVkLH\",\n    \"proofPurpose\": \"assertionMethod\",\n    \"proofValue\": \"z2BWSF2efWCGXfUSVsehTVvT3fNor1XTnjxEhnN1p6qFsDjp5rWBbHJZyZmL2uhFqQEQ4iQNiLe1E75LV7vKWyaUw\"\n  },\n  \"id\": \"urn:prm:response:uEiDFeTKTXvK8dDuBd3ND7SpnlD7Ntx-b17MRA8TArvc_Aw\"\n}",
    "verification/instructions.txt": "HOW TO VERIFY THIS BUNDLE\n=========================\n\nVerification displayed by PRM is provided for convenience. The underlying artifacts are independently verifiable without PRM.\n\nNothing below requires the PRM website, an account, or a network connection.\n\n\n1. EVERYTHING AT ONCE\n\n   npx @prm/cli verify notice.prmproof\n\n   Exit code 0 means verified, 1 means verified with warnings (for example, no\n   timestamp evidence was included), 2 means it failed.\n\n\n2. WHAT THAT CHECKS\n\n   - manifest.json lists every artifact with the SHA-256 of its exact bytes.\n     Each one is recomputed and compared.\n   - The manifest itself is hashed and compared against the bundle's\n     manifestDigest, so a single altered entry is detected.\n   - policy.json is checked against its own signature.\n   - key-events/kel.json is walked from its genesis event. The account\n     identifier is recomputed from that event, so identity is not taken on\n     trust from anyone, including PRM.\n   - notice.json, if present, is checked against its signature and confirmed to\n     reference the policy in this bundle by BOTH digests.\n   - Delivery and response records, if present, are checked against their\n     signatures and their references.\n\n\n3. TWO DIGESTS, AND WHY BOTH ARE RECORDED\n\n   Policy digest  Identifies the DOCUMENT. It is computed over a canonical form,\n                  so reformatting the JSON does not change it.\n   Byte digest    Identifies the exact BYTES. Reformatting does change it.\n\n   A reserialized policy keeps its policy digest but gets a different byte\n   digest. Recording both lets you show not only which policy was issued, but\n   which exact file was delivered.\n\n\n4. TIMESTAMP EVIDENCE, IF PRESENT\n\n   Tokens under timestamps/ are RFC 3161 and are base64 encoded. To check one\n   with standard tooling:\n\n     base64 -d < timestamps/<name> > token.tsr\n     openssl ts -reply -in token.tsr -text          # read it\n     openssl ts -verify -in token.tsr \\\n       -queryfile <query> -CAfile <tsa-chain.pem>   # verify it\n\n   The token attests that the referenced hash existed no later than the time it\n   states. It says nothing about who created the content, which is what the\n   signature above is for.\n\n\n5. IF SOMETHING FAILS\n\n   Any mismatch means the bundle you have is not the bundle that was produced.\n   Report exactly which check failed; the tool names the artifact and both\n   digests.\n",
    "README.txt": "PRM PROOF BUNDLE\n================\n\nThis file is a portable evidence package. It contains a signed personal data\npolicy and, where applicable, the notice that was sent about it, a record of how\nand when it was delivered, and any response that came back.\n\nWHAT IT ESTABLISHES\n\n  - what policy the issuer signed, and which exact bytes\n  - when that policy took effect\n  - which recipient a notice was directed to, if any\n  - when and how the issuer recorded delivering it\n  - what response, if any, the issuer recorded afterwards\n\nWHAT IT DOES NOT DO\n\n  This package records a person's stated instructions and objections. It does not\n  create legal rights or obligations that do not otherwise exist, and it does not\n  override a court order, a statutory mandate, or other controlling authority.\n\n  The delivery time is asserted by the issuer. PRM does not witness delivery and\n  makes no claim to. Independent corroboration, where present, comes from\n  transparency log inclusion and timestamp tokens.\n\n  A response record preserves what the recipient said and how the issuer\n  characterised it. PRM does not decide whether the recipient's position is\n  correct.\n\nCONTENTS\n\n  manifest.json                the integrity map: every artifact and its digest\n  policy.json                  the signed policy\n  key-events/kel.json          the issuer key history\n  notice.json                  the recipient-specific notice\n  policy-chain/                1 earlier version(s)\n  delivery/                    signed delivery record(s)\n  response/                    signed response record(s)\n  log/signed-tree-head.json    transparency log head\n  verification/instructions.txt  how to check all of it yourself\n\nTO VERIFY\n\n  npx @prm/cli verify notice.prmproof\n\n  Verification displayed by PRM is provided for convenience. The underlying artifacts are independently verifiable without PRM.\n",
    "manifest.json": "{\n  \"prmproof\": 2,\n  \"generatedAt\": \"2026-09-24T17:00:00Z\",\n  \"subject\": {\n    \"accountId\": \"prm:s2nfbcv7jr5kcf3yopfs5dlrqa\",\n    \"policyChainId\": \"urn:prm:chain:uEiDvRgzy0aV11g-h-BuMD9gbYTrA3EP7eKrFyeOeyn_VGw\",\n    \"policyDigest\": \"uEiCCVYqo5goptwm4lS1RN_8WgOwJ5A8un4JTasreIyS9JA\",\n    \"policyByteDigest\": \"uEiCKt6706NwzOf5Som7k6H20_z_DEh6Gwq8rH-IhM8yEeQ\",\n    \"policyVersion\": 1,\n    \"noticeDigest\": \"uEiC5IVcL4rLIEItGi5JPCBeTyfp__1e7h9yL3Z_vJO3tRg\"\n  },\n  \"entries\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"README.txt\",\n      \"byteDigest\": \"uEiBzVD_qd2OEJHipKKJv3cg1egM5m1VZYZxsmhpUh8uiyw\",\n      \"byteLength\": 1878,\n      \"contentType\": \"text/plain\",\n      \"description\": \"Plain-language description of this bundle.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"delivery/delivery-1.json\",\n      \"byteDigest\": \"uEiAAPiLY9UiHmaNyx9b5Mf2fLsfNVWYPeWoSG8oyiRLBxA\",\n      \"byteLength\": 1197,\n      \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n      \"description\": \"Signed delivery record. The delivery time is asserted by the issuer, not witnessed by PRM.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"key-events/kel.json\",\n      \"byteDigest\": \"uEiCfm2NeONPx2DYc_u1FlyAwOVjMPggARvUodSAz2dZ8Pw\",\n      \"byteLength\": 1217,\n      \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n      \"description\": \"The issuer key history. Proves the signing key was authorized, and that the account identifier derives from its own genesis event.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"log/ledger.json\",\n      \"byteDigest\": \"uEiA2QOBX8XQXpcHe9VS12HQhTdczb7Hi_Ijhio1PVPVwpw\",\n      \"byteLength\": 6475,\n      \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n      \"description\": \"Personal ledger entries relevant to this notice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"log/signed-tree-head.json\",\n      \"byteDigest\": \"uEiAhdX8dgrkUrleBQ1DG7Foyzchv7LCgvSsZxGz98Awfkw\",\n      \"byteLength\": 260,\n      \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n      \"description\": \"Transparency log head. With an inclusion proof, shows the entry was logged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"notice.json\",\n      \"byteDigest\": \"uEiCIyPjwICpDnmZkPXEHbvQVJftRXjhiagXZrSzs0I1ibg\",\n      \"byteLength\": 2656,\n      \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n      \"description\": \"The recipient-specific notice. References the policy by both digests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"policy-chain/v1.json\",\n      \"byteDigest\": \"uEiCKt6706NwzOf5Som7k6H20_z_DEh6Gwq8rH-IhM8yEeQ\",\n      \"byteLength\": 8869,\n      \"contentType\": \"application/prm-policy+json\",\n      \"description\": \"Policy version 1, retained so the version chain can be walked offline.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"policy.json\",\n      \"byteDigest\": \"uEiCKt6706NwzOf5Som7k6H20_z_DEh6Gwq8rH-IhM8yEeQ\",\n      \"byteLength\": 8869,\n      \"contentType\": \"application/prm-policy+json\",\n      \"description\": \"The signed policy, exactly as published. This is the authoritative document.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"response/response-1.json\",\n      \"byteDigest\": \"uEiDwqDeJyP_rFMMbLcDpua_m920Sw8eZlk1-kMKoxAxMjA\",\n      \"byteLength\": 1083,\n      \"contentType\": \"application/json\",\n      \"description\": \"Signed response record. Preserves what came back; PRM does not evaluate it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"verification/instructions.txt\",\n      \"byteDigest\": \"uEiDfE771GA02N2X1AHs86GPP5jj5qRvxwV4lcfm7trwGzA\",\n      \"byteLength\": 2401,\n      \"contentType\": \"text/plain\",\n      \"description\": \"How to verify everything in this bundle without contacting PRM.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
  }
}